cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the two
  papers that introduced mTDR (listed under references).
type: software
title: "mtdr: model-based targeted dimensionality reduction in Python"
abstract: >-
  A Python port of model-based targeted dimensionality reduction (mTDR), which
  fits neural population activity as a sum of low-rank, time-varying regression
  coefficient matrices, one per task variable, with ranks chosen by AIC and
  support for non-simultaneously recorded neurons.
authors:
  - family-names: Yanar
    given-names: Jorge
    affiliation: Princeton University
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jyanar/mtdr"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-08"
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - dimensionality reduction
  - reduced-rank regression
  - neural population
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Prefrontal cortex exhibits multidimensional dynamic encoding during
      decision-making
    authors:
      - family-names: Aoi
        given-names: Mikio C.
      - family-names: Mante
        given-names: Valerio
      - family-names: Pillow
        given-names: Jonathan W.
    journal: Nature Neuroscience
    volume: 23
    start: 1410
    end: 1420
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1038/s41593-020-0696-5
  - type: conference-paper
    title: Model-based targeted dimensionality reduction for neuronal population data
    authors:
